TEXT 264 -32 Left 2 ;You can draw the powerlostline of Z_r :\n ALT+ left mouseklick to the Z_r device \nThe result is the 1~ powerlost -> edit and multiply the expression in the graphic\nby 3 to get the 3~ lost\nor:\nplot v(r_p1)+v(r_p2)\n \nHint: If you plot the powerlost with the first method it will be displayed with a \nright y-axis in unit MW\nWith the second method the powerlost is displayed with a left y-axis in unit MV\nIf you mix this two methods be sure that both y-axis have the same ymin and\nymax values
TEXT -232 360 Left 2 ;Result:\n \nYou can see that the voltage (ld_v = voltage on constant power element ) decreases with the increasing power of the load  \nThe shape of the Voltage ld_v is linear at the beginning and later exponential\n \nAt the point of approximately 60kV the circuit cannot converge because a voltage breakdown occur.\nsee also the power lost curve at Z_r \n \nThe powerlost at Z_r at the end of the simulation ( when the voltage breakdown occur ) is as high as the power of the load !!!
